Hi, Franki,
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">I wanted to share this with you so you know where my head=
 is at.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">Today I worked a double at the welcome center because all=
 the other hosts left. It was my last day there. John spent three hours wit=
h me, so he got to see me in this role firsthand=97I hope you=92ll ask him =
about it.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">This is what I want to do. I feel valued in this role. I =
help people. I elevate their experiences at these parks. They like me. Over=
 and over, guests tell me how glad they are that I was the one who helped t=
hem. This isn=92t performative=97it=92s
 real. John witnessed this.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">It=92s what I=92ll be doing at Beverly Beach, and I=92m e=
xcited for it. But there are a lot of months in between. I=92ve reached out=
 to South Beach, Nehalem Bay, and Cape Lookout. None of those VSLs have res=
ponded, and Logan isn=92t helping.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">My work ethic is undeniable. My contributions are undenia=
ble. I bring value to everything I touch.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
<div dir=3D"auto">Will you help me? I want to work in welcome centers. Bull=
ards Beach is another possibility. Maybe other parks I haven=92t considered=
? And Umpqua=97because I value my connection to you, and I won=92t let that=
 disintegrate, even if it means cleaning
 yurts.</div>
<div dir=3D"auto"><br>
</div>
Samuel
